---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";
import Pairing from "../../components/Pairing.astro";
import { BASE } from "../../config.ts";
---
<Base
  title="Tarot card combinations: read two cards together · ShenTarot"
  description="Pick any two tarot cards, upright or reversed, and see how they read together: theme and detail, suits, numbers, court cards and elements. Free, in your browser."
  path="tools/combinations"
  crumbs={[["Free tools", "tools"], ["Card combinations", "tools/combinations"]]}
>
  <header class="page-head center">
    <p class="eyebrow">Free tool</p>
    <h1>Tarot card combinations</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Pick two cards from a reading, or draw two at random, and see what links them: which one sets the theme, what
      their suits, numbers and elements say, and a question from each card to reflect on.
    </p>
  </header>
  <Pairing mode="combine" slots={["First card", "Second card"]} />
  <section class="narrow" style="margin:3rem auto 0">
    <h2>How to read two cards together</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Read each card on its own first, then ask how one changes the other. The second card often answers or qualifies the first.</li>
      <li>A Major Arcana card carries more weight. When it sits next to a Minor Arcana card, the Major names the theme and the Minor shows how it shows up.</li>
      <li>Try one sentence that holds both meanings. If it feels forced, look at the picture on each card for a detail they share.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="muted">For entertainment and self-reflection. See also <a href={`${BASE}tools/elements`}>elemental dignities</a> and <a href={`${BASE}cards`}>all 78 card meanings</a>.</p>
  </section>
</Base>
